{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "init:i1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "The init node corresponds to the temporal opening of the first unit."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process. However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The XOR branch and its two guards accurately model the two alternative initiation conditions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the counting and comparison action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n5",
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "guard:b2->n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process. However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process. Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "The branch and guards correctly segment the three mutually exclusive order status conditions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process. However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process. Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the specific instruction to email the customer regarding damage and charges."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process. Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards faithfully represent the packing vs. storage decision."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact match for the missing-item notification step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact match for the inventory removal step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b4->n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process. However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards match the customer return evaluation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b5->n12",
        "guard:b5->n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process. On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards correctly model the repair feasibility check."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process. On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the positive repair path action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process. On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the negative repair path combining discard and notification."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order. If the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process. If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards match the final disposition routing."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Action and end node align with the explicit termination statement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The customer is then emailed with replacement charges, and the process is complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the final completion clause."
    }
